# Copy to compose/develop/.env before running any `make` target.
# Every Makefile target passes --env-file compose/develop/.env; without this
# file docker compose aborts before starting anything.

# --- HuggingFace ---------------------------------------------------------
# Needed for gated repos (FLUX, Llama, Gemma). Read-only token is enough:
# https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens
HF_TOKEN=

# --- Postgres ------------------------------------------------------------
# Consumed by the `db` service and interpolated into DB_URL for the sprite
# services. Changing these after first boot requires wiping
# compose/develop/db/data/ — init.sql only runs on an empty data dir.
DB_USER=postgres
DB_PASSWORD=password
DB_NAME=llm_monitoring

# --- Compute -------------------------------------------------------------
# cpu | cuda. Normally you do NOT set this by hand: docker-compose.cuda.yml
# forces COMPUTE_DEVICE=cuda on the worker when nvidia-smi is present on the
# host. Set it here only to pin the worker to CPU on a GPU machine.
# COMPUTE_DEVICE=cpu

# Host-visible bind address for the sprite API. 127.0.0.1 keeps it local;
# 0.0.0.0 exposes it to the LAN (see "Home-network exposure" in README).
SPRITE_API_BIND=127.0.0.1

# --- Storage -------------------------------------------------------------
# Model weights and generated images. Defaults (../../models, ../../images)
# put them next to the repo, which on this setup lives under /mnt/c — a 9p
# mount where loading multi-GB weights is painfully slow.
#
# Point these at the WSL ext4 filesystem instead. Absolute paths only.
#   MODELS_DIR=/home/<you>/sprite-data/models
#
# IMAGES_DIR is the exception: generated PNGs are small and written once, so
# the 9p penalty is negligible (~20ms for a 1MB file) and keeping them in the
# project makes them visible in Explorer and the IDE. Measured: 9p writes at
# 48MB/s vs ext4 54MB/s. It is model weights and the DB that must not go there
# (9p reads 44MB/s vs ext4 cached 3.9GB/s; 2000 small files 17.5s vs 0.5s).
MODELS_DIR=../../models
IMAGES_DIR=../../images

# Generated audio (music, ambience, sfx). Small files, same reasoning as
# IMAGES_DIR, so the in-repo default is fine. Listed because compose only
# defaults it (${AUDIO_DIR:-../../audio}) and it is easy to miss that the
# Audio tab writes anywhere at all.
AUDIO_DIR=../../audio

# NOTHING HERE DOWNLOADS MODEL WEIGHTS. Not `make up`, not `make build`.
# Point MODELS_DIR at ext4 first, then run:
#     make provision dry=1     # what is missing, and how big
#     make provision           # the required tier, 56.4 GB
#     make provision tier=all  # every optional feature, 103 GB
# Declared in compose/develop/downloader/models.toml. See
# .ai/decisions/0014 and .ai/specs/model-provisioning/.
# `models.txt` is the retired llama.cpp router's lane and is not this.

# --- Auth ----------------------------------------------------------------
# LEGACY shared secret, still honoured by auth.py as one valid credential.
# Leave it EMPTY and use minted keys instead: `make api-key`.
#
# Read the rule carefully, because "empty = no auth" is only half true:
#
#     enforced = bool(SPRITE_API_TOKEN) or active_keys > 0
#
# So a brand-new deploy with this empty and no keys yet IS open - that is the
# bootstrap that lets you mint the first key. The moment that key exists the
# API is enforced on EVERY route that spends GPU time or lists images, which
# includes plain <img src="/api/jobs/{id}/sheet"> tags and every helper script
# that does not send a bearer. Check with `GET /api/auth/mode`.
#
# Scripts read the minted key from SPRITE_API_KEY (written by `make api-key`,
# not set here). Export it before running them:
#     export SPRITE_API_KEY=$(grep '^SPRITE_API_KEY=' compose/develop/.env | cut -d= -f2-)
#
# If you do set this, register it in something2's provider config as header
# "Authorization" with token "Bearer <this value>".
SPRITE_API_TOKEN=

# Must stay BELOW something2's AI_PROVIDER_GENERATE_TIMEOUT_MS (default 5 min)
# so a slow job surfaces as our 504 rather than their opaque timeout.
A1111_GENERATE_TIMEOUT_S=285

# --- Model gateway -------------------------------------------------------
# A model selected in the UI holds the GPU until it has been idle this long;
# jobs for other models wait (UI) or get 503 + Retry-After (something2) until
# then. Also the longest any model can hold the card against an older job.
MODEL_SWITCH_IDLE_S=300
# How often a deferred job re-checks whether it may run.
MODEL_GATEWAY_RECHECK_S=5

# Postgres data directory. Like MODELS_DIR, this must live on the WSL ext4
# filesystem — a /mnt/c bind mount breaks initdb's permission handling.
#   DB_DATA_DIR=/home/<you>/sprite-data/db
DB_DATA_DIR=./db/data

# --- Image editing (POST /api/edit) --------------------------------------
# Off by default. An edit takes the whole card for its duration and the model
# gateway hands it the same slot as an hour-long sheet build, so it is opt-in.
#
# Note the spelling. EDIT_ENABLE (no D) is read by NOTHING: set that and `env`
# inside the container shows it while /api/edit keeps answering 503. Compose
# passes it to BOTH sprite-generator and sprite-worker, because the API
# answers that 503 from the same constant the worker reads, and the containers
# must be RECREATED rather than restarted for it to take effect.
#
# Runs Qwen-Image-Edit-2511 (GGUF + Lightning), which needs no extra download
# on a host that can already build sheets. See .ai/decisions/0015 - including
# its "Known limits": this re-renders the whole image, so it is for large
# frame-filling subjects and not for repairing a concept.
EDIT_ENABLED=0
# "flux-nf4" switches back to the retired FLUX Kontext path, whose weights are
# [[dead]] in models.toml and are NOT fetched by `make provision`.
# EDIT_ENGINE=qwen-gguf
# An edit that recomposes instead of editing is retried on a fresh seed, up to
# this many times; the bound is result-opaque-share / source-opaque-share.
# Only meaningful for a source WITH alpha. See 0015 "The reframe guard".
# EDIT_ATTEMPTS=3
# EDIT_FRAMING_TOLERANCE=1.6
